# Vercel AI SDK Best Practices

## Version Notice

**This project uses AI SDK v5.** Be aware of the differences between v5 and v6 (beta):

### AI SDK v5 (Current)

- Import from: `@ai-sdk/react` (for hooks), `ai` (for core functions)
- `useChat()` returns: `{ messages, sendMessage, status }`
- Status values: `'ready' | 'submitted' | 'streaming' | 'error'`
- Messages have `.parts` array (not `.content`)
- API route returns: `result.toUIMessageStreamResponse()`
- Use `convertToModelMessages()` to convert UIMessages
- Transport: `new DefaultChatTransport({ api: '/api/chat' })`

### AI SDK v6 Beta

- Import from: `ai` (unified package)
- Different API signatures
- Different return types
- `toDataStreamResponse()` instead of `toUIMessageStreamResponse()`

**Always refer to AI SDK v5 documentation for this project.**

## Installation & Setup

- Install AI SDK: `pnpm add ai`
- Install React hooks: `pnpm add @ai-sdk/react`
- Install provider: `pnpm add @ai-sdk/openai` (or other providers)
- Store API keys in `.env.local`
- Never commit API keys to version control
- Use environment variables: `OPENAI_API_KEY`, `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`, etc.
- Set `maxDuration` in route handlers for streaming responses

## Route Handlers (API Routes)

- Create API routes in `app/api/` directory
- Use `POST` method for AI requests
- Set proper `maxDuration` for streaming (e.g., 30s)
- Use `streamText()` for text generation
- Use `convertToModelMessages()` to convert UIMessage[] to model format
- Return `result.toUIMessageStreamResponse()` for v5 streaming
- Import types: `type UIMessage` from `ai`

### Example API Route (v5)

```typescript
import { openai } from "@ai-sdk/openai";
import { streamText, convertToModelMessages, type UIMessage } from "ai";

export const maxDuration = 30;

export async function POST(req: Request) {
  const { messages }: { messages: UIMessage[] } = await req.json();

  const result = streamText({
    model: openai("gpt-4o-mini"),
    messages: convertToModelMessages(messages),
  });

  return result.toUIMessageStreamResponse();
}
```

## Client-Side Hooks

### useChat() (v5)

- Import from `@ai-sdk/react`
- Returns: `{ messages, sendMessage, status, stop }`
- `messages`: Array of UIMessage with `.parts` property
- `sendMessage()`: Send message with `{ text: string }`
- `status`: `'ready' | 'submitted' | 'streaming' | 'error'`
- Use `DefaultChatTransport` to configure API endpoint
- Automatically manages message history
- Handles streaming responses

### Example useChat (v5)

```typescript
import { useChat } from "@ai-sdk/react";
import { DefaultChatTransport } from "ai";

const { messages, sendMessage, status } = useChat({
  transport: new DefaultChatTransport({
    api: "/api/chat",
  }),
});

// Send a message
sendMessage({ text: "Hello AI!" });

// Check status
const isLoading = status === "streaming" || status === "submitted";

// Render messages
messages.map((message) => (
  <div key={message.id}>
    {message.parts.map((part, i) =>
      part.type === "text" ? <span key={i}>{part.text}</span> : null
    )}
  </div>
));
```

### useCompletion()

- Use for text completion interfaces
- Provides `completion`, `input`, `handleSubmit`, `isLoading`
- Streams text token by token
- Good for writing assistants, autocomplete

### useObject()

- Use for generating structured data
- Validates against Zod schemas
- Returns typed objects
- Good for forms, data extraction

## Message Structure (v5)

### UIMessage Format

```typescript
{
  id: string;
  role: 'user' | 'assistant' | 'system';
  parts: Array<{
    type: 'text' | 'tool-invocation' | 'tool-result' | ...;
    text?: string;  // For text parts
    // ... other part-specific properties
  }>;
}
```

**Important:** Messages have `.parts` array, not `.content` string!

## AI Providers

### OpenAI

- Use `@ai-sdk/openai`
- Models: `gpt-4o`, `gpt-4o-mini`, `gpt-3.5-turbo`
- Best for general-purpose tasks
- Good streaming performance

### Anthropic

- Use `@ai-sdk/anthropic`
- Models: `claude-3-5-sonnet`, `claude-3-opus`, `claude-3-haiku`
- Excellent for reasoning and analysis
- Strong context handling

### Google

- Use `@ai-sdk/google`
- Models: `gemini-pro`, `gemini-pro-vision`
- Good for multimodal tasks

### Custom Providers

- Use `@ai-sdk/provider` for custom implementations
- Support for local models (Ollama, LM Studio)
- Can wrap any OpenAI-compatible API

## Streaming

- Always use streaming for better UX
- Set `maxDuration` in route config
- Use `streamText()` for text responses
- Handle loading states in UI with `status` from `useChat()`
- Show typing indicators during streaming
- Implement proper error boundaries
- Check `status === 'streaming'` for active streaming

## Structured Outputs

- Use `generateObject()` with Zod schemas
- Validate responses automatically
- Type-safe outputs
- Good for forms, data extraction, function calling

### Example with Zod

```typescript
import { z } from "zod";
import { generateObject } from "ai";

const schema = z.object({
  name: z.string(),
  age: z.number(),
  email: z.string().email(),
});

const { object } = await generateObject({
  model: openai("gpt-4o-mini"),
  schema,
  prompt: "Generate user data",
});
```

## Tool Calling (Function Calling)

- Define tools with Zod schemas
- Execute functions based on AI responses
- Return results back to AI
- Implement multi-turn conversations
- Handle tool errors gracefully

### Tool Definition

```typescript
const weatherTool = {
  description: "Get weather for a location",
  parameters: z.object({
    location: z.string(),
  }),
  execute: async ({ location }) => {
    return `Weather in ${location}: Sunny`;
  },
};
```

